# Vendored acme worked-example repo — a full stele graph whose nodes, anchors, and quoted
# anchor syntax would pollute this repo's own graph if scanned (SPEC §2.4 dogfood).
tests/fixtures/
# CI plumbing, not architecture — kept out of the graph so its tracked dot-dir needs no
# node and never trips exhaustiveness (§4.3).
.github/
# The published GitHub Pages site (the design page, the guide and its figures)
# — presentation, not architecture, so it needs no node and never trips §4.3.
# docs/spec.html stays scanned: it is the contract, and the root's outranks claim
# anchors its decision-log landmark there.
docs/*
!docs/spec.html
